     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Passive voice puts the person or thing something happened TO in subject position (*Cortés fue recibido...*), which is exactly what a narrative needs when the receiver of the action matters more than the doer, or when the doer changes sentence to sentence. Compare it with active voice — *Moctezuma recibió a Cortés* — which shifts the emphasis entirely."
