 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.conquista.05.voz-pasiva-fuentes",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva: interpretación histórica",
+  "title": "Opinions: creer que and no creer que",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "When a text talks about how history itself gets written — who wrote a source, who compiled it, who promoted an interpretation — passive voice keeps the focus on the source or the idea, with por naming the author only when it matters. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *creo que* + indicative and *no creo que* + subjunctive from B1 Unit 7; the same rule works for *creen que* and *no creen que*. They are the natural tools for a debate among historians: say whose opinion it is, then use the right mood."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Mood after creer",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "Algunos historiadores creen que conquista es la palabra correcta.",
+          "*creen que* + indicative (*es*)."
+        ],
+        [
+          "Otros no creen que esta palabra explique todo.",
+          "*no creen que* + subjunctive (*explique*)."
+        ],
+        [
