         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Los pocos testimonios indígenas que sobrevivieron fueron recopilados y traducidos siglos después por Miguel León-Portilla.",
-          "english": "The few indigenous testimonies that survived were compiled and translated centuries later by Miguel León-Portilla."
+          "spanish": "Otros no creen que esta palabra explique todo.",
+          "english": "Others do not believe that this word explains everything."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Durante mucho tiempo fue promovida, sobre todo en España, una interpretación conocida como 'leyenda blanca'.",
-          "english": "For a long time, an interpretation known as the 'white legend' was promoted, especially in Spain."
+          "spanish": "Muchos historiadores creen que las enfermedades mataron a muchas personas.",
+          "english": "Many historians believe that diseases killed many people."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Ambas leyendas fueron construidas, en última instancia, con fines políticos más que históricos.",
-          "english": "Both legends were built, ultimately, for political rather than historical purposes."
+          "spanish": "Algunos historiadores no creen que la leyenda negra sea falsa por completo.",
+          "english": "Some historians do not believe that the black legend is completely false."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Notice that none of these sentences needs a por phrase to make sense — *leyenda blanca* *fue promovida* works fine without saying by whom, because the point is that it existed and shaped opinion, not exactly who pushed it hardest. Passive voice lets you make that choice sentence by sentence."
+      "content": "In a debate about the past, always attribute the opinion (*algunos historiadores creen que…*, *otros no creen que…*) instead of giving your own. *Creer que* accepts the idea (indicative); *no creer que* doubts it (subjunctive)."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-economiacolonial-01-extraccion-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-economiacolonial-01-extraccion-gr.json
