 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.economiacolonial.02.trabajo",
-  "title": "Se pasivo: sistemas de trabajo colonial",
+  "title": "Impersonal se: who was forced to work",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The *se*-passive fits labor systems perfectly: a practice that was granted, demanded, or replaced by policy over time, not a single person's one-time decision. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know impersonal *se* from B1 Unit 6 (*se trabaja mucho aquí*): the verb stays singular when there is no noun to agree with. With a person after *a*, it works the same way: *se obligaba a los indígenas a trabajar*. It leaves out who did the forcing, which suits the history of forced labour."
