 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.sociedadcolonial.02.jerarquia",
-  "title": "Se pasiva / impersonal: jerarquía colonial",
+  "title": "Relative clauses with a preposition: groups and hierarchy",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The se-passive is especially good at describing a sustained pattern of exclusion or requirement — something that kept happening, not a single decision by one named authority. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know relative clauses with a preposition (*el edificio en el que vivimos*, *la avería de la que hablamos*, *los vecinos con los que hablé*) from B1 Unit 20. They are useful for describing colonial groups: the group a person belonged to, the society they lived in, the authorities they depended on."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Preposition + article + que",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "el grupo al que pertenecía una persona",
+          "*pertenecer a* + *el que* (a + el = al)"
+        ],
+        [
+          "la sociedad en la que vivían",
+          "*vivir en* + *la que*"
+        ],
+        [
+          "las autoridades de las que dependían",
+          "*depender de* + *las que*"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "En la práctica, se favorecía sistemáticamente a la 'república de españoles' sobre la 'república de indios'.",
-          "english": "In practice, the 'republic of Spaniards' was systematically favored over the 'republic of Indians'."
+          "spanish": "El grupo al que pertenecía una persona influía en sus derechos.",
+          "english": "The group a person belonged to affected their rights."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Para acceder a la universidad o a un cargo público, se exigía presentar un certificado de 'limpieza de sangre'.",
-          "english": "To gain access to university or a public post, a 'blood purity' certificate had to be presented."
+          "spanish": "La sociedad en la que vivían estaba dividida en grupos.",
+          "english": "The society they lived in was divided into groups."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Se reservaban los cargos más altos casi exclusivamente para los peninsulares.",
-          "english": "The highest posts were reserved almost exclusively for those born in Spain."
+          "spanish": "Los indígenas tenían autoridades de las que no dependían los españoles.",
+          "english": "The indigenous people had authorities that the Spaniards did not depend on."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Con el tiempo, se acumuló tanto resentimiento en torno a esta exclusión que buena parte del liderazgo independentista saldría de esas familias.",
-          "english": "Over time, so much resentment built up around this exclusion that much of the independence leadership would come from those very families."
+          "spanish": "El lugar en el que vivía una persona también contaba.",
+          "english": "The place where a person lived also counted."
         }
