 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.sociedadcolonial.03.iglesia",
-  "title": "Gerundio: religión y sociedad colonial",
+  "title": "Para que + subjunctive: why the Church did things",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The gerund is the natural tool for showing two things happening at once — a missionary teaching while learning a language, a community producing goods while developing a musical tradition. It can open the sentence or sit right after the subject. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *para que* + subjunctive from B1 Unit 4 (*para que no pierdas la oportunidad*): it gives the purpose of an action when the people involved are different. Texts about the colony often use the present for past events, so the subjunctive after *para que* is in the present too."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Different subjects or the same",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "Los frailes aprenden lenguas para que los indígenas entiendan el mensaje.",
+          "two subjects: *para que* + subjunctive"
+        ],
+        [
+          "Los frailes aprenden lenguas para entender a los indígenas.",
+          "one subject: *para* + infinitive"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Enseñando la doctrina cristiana mientras aprendían y usaban el idioma guaraní, los jesuitas lograron una relación menos violenta.",
-          "english": "Teaching Christian doctrine while learning and using the Guaraní language, the Jesuits achieved a less violent relationship."
+          "spanish": "El papa da ese derecho a los reyes para que lleven el cristianismo a las nuevas tierras.",
+          "english": "The pope gives that right to the kings so that they bring Christianity to the new lands."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Estas comunidades, produciendo tejidos y ganado mientras desarrollaban una notable tradición musical, llegaron a ser económicamente prósperas.",
-          "english": "These communities, producing textiles and cattle while developing a notable musical tradition, became economically prosperous."
+          "spanish": "Los frailes aprenden lenguas indígenas para que los indígenas entiendan el mensaje.",
+          "english": "The friars learn indigenous languages so that the indigenous people understand the message."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las reducciones, dependiendo casi por completo de la administración jesuita, entraron en rápida decadencia tras la expulsión.",
-          "english": "The missions, depending almost entirely on Jesuit administration, fell into rapid decline after the expulsion."
+          "spanish": "Se fundan universidades para que los jóvenes estudien en América.",
+          "english": "Universities are founded so that young people study in America."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Vigilando la ortodoxia religiosa mientras construía hospitales, escuelas y universidades, la Iglesia funcionó como una de las instituciones más poderosas del imperio.",
-          "english": "Monitoring religious orthodoxy while building hospitals, schools and universities, the Church functioned as one of the empire's most powerful institutions."
+          "spanish": "Los frailes escriben gramáticas para aprender mejor las lenguas.",
