 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.sociedadcolonial.04.vida-cotidiana",
-  "title": "Conectores formales: vida cotidiana colonial",
+  "title": "Frequency adverbs: daily life in the plaza",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A lo largo del día orders daily activity across a stretch of time; *a raíz de* and como consecuencia de both introduce a cause, with como consecuencia de leaning slightly more formal and conclusive. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *siempre*, *a veces* and *nunca*, and from B1 Unit 12 *normalmente*, *a menudo*, *de vez en cuando* and *cada día*. In a description of colonial life they go with the imperfect, which tells how things used to happen."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "How often?",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "siempre",
+          "always"
+        ],
+        [
+          "normalmente",
+          "usually"
+        ],
+        [
+          "a menudo",
+          "often"
+        ],
+        [
+          "a veces",
+          "sometimes"
+        ],
+        [
+          "de vez en cuando",
+          "from time to time"
+        ],
+        [
+          "nunca",
+          "never"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "A raíz de las Leyes de Indias, promulgadas en 1573, prácticamente todas las nuevas ciudades siguieron el mismo patrón.",
-          "english": "As a result of the Laws of the Indies, issued in 1573, practically every new city followed the same pattern."
+          "spanish": "Normalmente, los vecinos iban a la plaza para comprar comida.",
+          "english": "Normally, the residents went to the plaza to buy food."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "A lo largo del día, esa plaza y sus alrededores se llenaban de actividad.",
-          "english": "Throughout the day, that plaza and its surroundings filled with activity."
+          "spanish": "A menudo, los vendedores llegaban de los pueblos vecinos.",
+          "english": "Often, the sellers came from the neighbouring towns."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Como consecuencia de esa actividad constante, la plaza funcionaba como el verdadero centro social de la ciudad.",
-          "english": "As a consequence of that constant activity, the plaza functioned as the city's true social center."
+          "spanish": "Cada día, el mercado era un lugar de trabajo y de noticias.",
+          "english": "Every day, the market was a place of work and news."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "La vida cotidiana colonial, a raíz de sus propias tensiones de género, de clase y de costumbre, generaba conflictos tan reales como los grandes debates políticos.",
-          "english": "Colonial daily life, due to its own tensions of gender, class and custom, generated conflicts as real as the great political debates."
