 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.sociedadcolonial.05.sintesis",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva: síntesis de la sociedad colonial",
+  "title": "Verbs of change: how colonial society changed",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "A synthesis paragraph often needs several passive sentences in a row, each treating a different institution as its subject — administration, opportunity, infrastructure — to show how they fit together without repeating 'the Spanish' as the agent every time. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the verbs of change (*ponerse*, *volverse*, *hacerse*, *quedarse*, *convertirse en*) from B1 Unit 25, and also *pasar de ser … a ser …*. They fit the story of the colony, where groups, cities and languages changed over time."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Which verb?",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "se convirtió en un hecho muy importante",
+          "*convertirse en* + noun: a big change"
+        ],
+        [
+          "se hicieron comerciantes",
+          "*hacerse* + noun: a change reached with time or effort"
+        ],
+        [
+          "se quedaron sin cargos importantes",
+          "*quedarse* + result"
+        ],
+        [
+          "pasaron de ser un grupo pequeño a ser un grupo grande",
+          "*pasar de ser … a ser …*"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Los territorios fueron administrados mediante virreinatos y audiencias que respondían a una corona lejana.",
-          "english": "The territories were administered through viceroyalties and high courts answering to a distant crown."
+          "spanish": "El mestizaje se convirtió en un hecho muy importante de la vida colonial.",
+          "english": "Mestizaje became a very important fact of colonial life."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las oportunidades económicas y políticas fueron distribuidas de forma muy desigual entre peninsulares, criollos, indígenas y africanos.",
-          "english": "Economic and political opportunities were distributed very unequally among peninsulares, criollos, indigenous people and Africans."
+          "spanish": "Algunos mestizos se hicieron comerciantes en las ciudades.",
+          "english": "Some mestizos became merchants in the cities."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las estructuras educativas y sanitarias fueron mantenidas, en gran medida, por una Iglesia que actuaba casi como un segundo gobierno.",
-          "english": "Educational and healthcare structures were maintained, to a large extent, by a Church that acted almost like a second government."
+          "spanish": "Los criollos pasaron de ser un grupo pequeño a ser un grupo grande.",
+          "english": "The criollos went from being a small group to being a large group."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Buena parte del trazado urbano actual fue diseñado directamente por una ley real de 1573.",
-          "english": "Much of today's urban layout was designed directly by a royal law of 1573."
+          "spanish": "Muchos criollos se quedaron sin cargos importantes.",
+          "english": "Many criollos were left without important posts."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "When you're summarizing a whole unit, passive voice lets each sentence open with the topic you're synthesizing (*los territorios*, *las oportunidades*, *las estructuras*) rather than forcing every sentence to start with '*España*' or '*la Corona*' — a small trick that keeps a synthesis paragraph from sounding repetitive."
+      "content": "Choose the verb by the kind of change: *convertirse en* for a big change, *hacerse* for something you become with time or effort, *quedarse* for a result, *pasar de ser … a ser …* to show both ends of the change."
     }
   ]
 }
